course: dictionary
lesson: 12287
title: Converge: coming together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Converge means to move towards each other and meet at one point. Lines, roads and rivers can converge. «The two roads converge at the old bridge.» The roads come together at the bridge, so converge means meet.
explain: People can converge too. «Fans converged on the stadium from every direction.» They came from different places and arrived at the same place. The clue from every direction tells you they came together.
explain: Ideas can converge as well: they become more alike. «Over time, their opinions began to converge.» Their views moved closer together. The opposite of converge is diverge, which means to move apart or become different.
fact: Converge means to come together and meet at one point.
fact: Converge is a verb, so its other forms are converges, converged and converging.
fact: «Converge on» a place means people arrive there from many directions.
fact: In maths, a sequence converges when its numbers get closer and closer to one fixed number.
fact: Converging lines in a drawing meet at one point far away, like railway tracks in a picture.
exercise: «The two rivers converge in the valley.» What does converge mean here? | *Meet at one point | Freeze solid | Dry up completely | Flow apart and go different ways
exercise: «Fans converged on the stadium from every direction.» Find and copy the word that shows the fans came together. | fans | direction | *converged | stadium
exercise: «Over time, their opinions began to converge.» What does this mean? | Their opinions were lost | They stopped talking | Their views became very different | *Their views became more alike
test: Which word means the opposite of converge? | Join | Gather | *Diverge | Meet
test: «The lines on the drawing seem to converge at the horizon.» What does converge mean? | *Meet at one point | Stay parallel forever | Break into pieces | Disappear
exam: In maths, a sequence converges when it gets closer and closer to what? | Zero only | A different random number each time | *One fixed number | Infinity forever
